      "markdown" : "# Queue notes",
      "warnings" : [

      ]
    },
    {
      "hash" : "1b6aff7befcd58",
      "index" : 1,
      "kind" : "paragraph",
      "markdown" : "The queue is basically ordered, and entries leave in the order they arrived.",
      "warnings" : [

      ]
    },
    {
      "hash" : "03f5af1f64f6dd",
      "index" : 2,
      "kind" : "paragraph",
      "markdown" : "The worker really quite simply retries a failed job once before it gives up.",
      "warnings" : [

      ]
    },
    {
      "hash" : "1c4c412b052878",
      "index" : 3,
      "kind" : "paragraph",
      "markdown" : "It should be noted that the retry path is unchanged from the previous release.",
      "warnings" : [

      ]
    },
    {
      "hash" : "034083ccb56163",
      "index" : 4,
      "kind" : "paragraph",
      "markdown" : "The scheduler just wakes every ten seconds and picks the oldest job.",
      "warnings" : [

      ]
    },
    {
      "hash" : "1964920d536ffc",
      "index" : 5,
      "kind" : "paragraph",
      "markdown" : "The **retry budget is basically fixed** at one attempt per job.",
      "warnings" : [

      ]
    },
    {
      "hash" : "092a2eb1fa62f0",
      "index" : 6,
      "kind" : "code",
      "markdown" : "```bash\nworker --retries 1 --basically-on\n```",
      "warnings" : [

      ]
